    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d30">

                <pb facs="0113" n="33" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg33"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. McCormick.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic">March 14,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 36.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of a letter asking whether
                    the widow of a man who served in the Austrian army live years is entitled to a
                    pension, or other gratuity, and, if so, what steps she must take to secure it.
                    You are instructed to obtain the desired information.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d30-a1.xml" xpointer="d30-a1"/>
